# Repo-root ignore rules.
#
# The subtrees keep their own, and those stay authoritative for their own contents:
#   Plugin/.gitignore        - VS/.NET build output, *.user, .vs/, Thunderstore/Packages/*.zip
#   UnityProject/.gitignore  - Library/, Temp/, Logs/, UserSettings/, generated csproj/sln
#   AssetSources/.gitignore  - Blender *.blend1 backups
#
# This file covers what none of them can: the repo root itself, and anything that
# turns up in a NEW top-level folder later. Without it, `git add -A` from the root
# reaches straight into the tool scratch directories below.

# Claude Code scratch. The agents and skills in .claude/ ARE meant to be tracked -
# a worktree is a full second checkout of this repo and must never be committed into it.
.claude/worktrees/

# Editor / IDE (both subtree ignores already exclude these for their own trees)
.vscode/
.idea/
*.suo
*.user
*.userosscache
*.sln.docstates

# Build output, wherever it appears
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/

# Python bytecode - the Audacity export scripts in AssetSources/Audio generate this
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.swp
# Editor backups. Written as *.*~ and NOT *~ on purpose: a bare *~ also matches Unity's
# `Documentation~` convention and would have ignored a tracked package folder.
*.*~
